<title>USA: Amer Home Products gets ok low dose pill.</title>
<headline>Amer Home Products gets ok low dose pill.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Home Products' Wyeth-Ayerst Laboratories division said that it has received clearance from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to market Alesse, a new low-dose birth control pill.</p>
<p>According to Wyeth-Ayerst, Alesse represents the lowest dose combination of levonorgestrel and ethinyl estradiol marketed in the United States.</p>
<p>The combination of levonorgestrel and ethinyl estradiol is the world's most widely prescribed birth control pill combination.</p>
</text>
